{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 20, :comments ["<b>Chavah.</b> An expression of liveliness, from the root היה הוה." "<b>Mother of all life.</b> Rabbi Simon said: mother of all the living. For all the one hundred and thirty years that Adam separated from Chavah, the male spirits would warm themselves from her and she would give birth from them, and the female spirits would warm themselves from him and give birth. As it is written: ״אשר בהעותו והוכחתיו בשבט אנשים.״ Another interpretation: <b>mother of all life</b> — an expression of greatness, as in 'I arose אם in Israel.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:02:45.033665702Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}